#. Screen reader announcement in the composer when two people are typing. {a} and {b} are their display names.
#: src/features/typing/rolling/RollingTypingText.tsx
msgid "{a} and {b} are typing..."
msgstr "{a} та {b} друкують..."

#. Screen reader announcement in the composer when one person is typing. {a} is their display name.
#: src/features/typing/rolling/RollingTypingText.tsx
msgid "{a} is typing..."
msgstr "{a} друкує..."

#. Screen reader announcement in the composer when three people are typing. {a}, {b} and {c} are their display names.
#: src/features/typing/rolling/RollingTypingText.tsx
msgid "{a}, {b} and {c} are typing..."
msgstr "{a}, {b} та {c} друкують..."

#. Activity log summary when a channel got a permission override for one member. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {user} is the member the override applies to, shown as a clickable user chip. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} added a permission override for {user} in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} додав(-ла) перевизначення дозволів для {user} у {channel}"

#. Activity log summary when a channel got a permission override for every member of the community. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. Keep @everyone unchanged. It is the name of the role that includes all members. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} added a permission override for @everyone in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} додав(-ла) перевизначення дозволів для @everyone у {channel}"

#. Activity log summary when a channel got a permission override for a role. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role, shown as a role chip with its name. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} added a permission override for the role {role} in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} додав(-ла) перевизначення дозволів для ролі {role} у {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for a sticker that was added to the community when its name was not recorded. {actor} is the member who added it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} added a sticker"
msgstr "{actor} додав(-ла) стікер"

#. Activity log summary for a custom emoji that was added to the community when its name was not recorded. {actor} is the member who added it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} added an emoji"
msgstr "{actor} додав(-ла) емодзі"

#. Activity log summary for a bot that was added to the community. {actor} is the member who added the bot, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the bot, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} added the bot {target}"
msgstr "{actor} додав(-ла) бота {target}"

#. Activity log summary for a bot that was added to the community with temporary membership. {actor} is the member who added the bot, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the bot, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} added the bot {target} as a temporary member"
msgstr "{actor} додав(-ла) бота {target} як тимчасового учасника"

#. Activity log summary for a custom emoji that was uploaded or copied to the community. {actor} is the member who added it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {emoji} is the emoji, shown as its image when it still exists, followed by its name between colons, for example :blobcat:.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} added the emoji {emoji}"
msgstr "{actor} додав(-ла) емодзі {emoji}"

#. Activity log summary for a sticker that was uploaded or copied to the community. {actor} is the member who added it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {name} is the sticker name, shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} added the sticker {name}"
msgstr "{actor} додав(-ла) стікер {name}"

#. Activity log summary for a user who was banned from the community with no end date. A ban removes the user from the community and stops them from joining again. It is not the feature that blocks a user. {actor} is the member who made the ban, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the banned user, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} banned {target}"
msgstr "{actor} заблокував(-ла) {target}"

#. Activity log summary for a user who was banned from the community for a limited time. A ban removes the user from the community and stops them from joining again. It is not the feature that blocks a user. {actor} is the member who made the ban, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the banned user, shown as a clickable user chip. {duration} is how long the ban lasts, shown as a formatted duration phrase such as "3 days" or "12 hours".
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} banned {target} for {duration}"
msgstr "{actor} заблокував(-ла) {target} на {duration}"

#. Activity log summary for a block on a member that was already running and was given a new end. The block stops the member from sending messages, reacting and joining voice, and it lifts on its own at the new end. Spell the effect out the way the English does. Do not name it with a word for a ban, a kick, a mute, a suspension or a waiting period, and do not say that time ran out. Keep the three things that are blocked. This is a past tense record of an action that already happened, never an instruction to the reader. {actor} is the member who moved the end of the block, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the blocked member, shown as a clickable user chip. {date} is the new end of the block, shown as a formatted date and time.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} changed {target}'s block on sending messages, reacting and joining voice to end at {date}"
msgstr "{actor} змінив(-ла) для {target} заборону надсилати повідомлення, реагувати та приєднуватися до голосових каналів: діє до {date}"

#. Activity log summary for a nickname that someone changed for another member in the community. {actor} is the member who changed the nickname, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member whose nickname changed, shown as a clickable user chip. {oldNick} is the previous nickname and {newNick} is the new nickname. Keep {oldNick} as the old value and {newNick} as the new value. The app shows both in bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} changed the nickname of {target} from {oldNick} to {newNick}"
msgstr "{actor} змінив(-ла) псевдонім для {target} з {oldNick} на {newNick}"

#. Activity log summary for an older entry that only recorded that the permission overrides of an announcement channel were changed, without saying which. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} changed the permission overrides of the announcement channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} змінив налаштування дозволів каналу оголошень {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for an older entry that only recorded that the permission overrides of a channel category were changed, without saying which. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the category, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} changed the permission overrides of the category {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} змінив(-ла) перевизначення дозволів для категорії {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for an older entry that only recorded that the permission overrides of a channel of a type this app version cannot name were changed, without saying which. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} changed the permission overrides of the channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} змінив(-ла) перевизначення дозволів для каналу {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for an entry that only recorded that the permission overrides of a forum channel were changed. {channel} is shown as a channel chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogForumPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} changed the permission overrides of the forum channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} змінив(ла) дозволи для форуму {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for an older entry that only recorded that the permission overrides of a link channel were changed, without saying which. A link channel is a channel list entry that opens a web address. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} changed the permission overrides of the link channel {channel}"
